--- A record of no fields, only declared, makes the compiled program not build.
--- Interpreted (crow run -i): prints "made" (and Body[] made and logged prints
--- "Body[]").
--- Compiled (crow run): the Rust compiler refuses the generated display code:
---     error[E0283]: type annotations needed
---       --> src/main.rs:35:56
---     error: the compiled program does not build — the Rust compiler refused what
---     Crow accepted, a bug in Crow, not in this program
--- The emitted impl is `crow_runtime::display::record("Body", vec![])`: an empty
--- vec! whose item type nothing names (the ToJson impl's `object(vec![])` is the
--- same shape). Expected: "made" in both modes (or the declaration refused in
--- both, if the spec meant a record to have a field — it does not say so).
--- Found writing rosetta/visitor_pattern.co (Wikipedia's car: Body and Engine
--- carry no data); worked around by giving them a name field.

struct Body []
log['made']
